<Layout title="About · Deep Hayer">
  <h1>About</h1>

  <p>
    I am Deep Hayer. I study applied math and business at Austin Community College.
    I was admitted at 12, finished two A.A. degrees in May 2026 (small business
    management and business administration), and finish a third in mathematics in
    December 2026.
  </p>

  <p>
    I build things and write about them. The work tends to sit at the intersection
    of applied math, finance, and behavioral psychology. Right now that means
    <a href="/projects/chalkiq">chalkIQ</a> (sports models),
    <a href="/projects/compiq">compIQ</a> (real estate comps),
    <a href="/projects/admittr">admittr</a> (admissions probability),
    <a href="/projects/hoi4">a HOI4 combat-model paper</a>, and
    <a href="/projects/redflag">redflag</a> (brand transparency).
  </p>

  <p>
    On this site I publish three kinds of things. Essays, which are exploratory and
    Montaigne-ish. Analysis, which is structured writing on sports, commercial real
    estate, M&amp;A, and finance. Notes, which are fragments, observations, and short
    pieces that do not deserve a longer treatment yet.
  </p>

  <p>
    Right now I am looking for internships in Austin: commercial real estate, family
    offices, boutique investment banks, and energy / power trading. If your team works
    on modeling, comps, underwriting, or anything where applied math meets dollars,
    <a href="mailto:deephayer940@gmail.com">email me</a>.
  </p>

